From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:47 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Plutonium: the shared module, and the contracts and
 keybindings it adds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Folded from:
- list agent-launched native windows under their thread
- per-thread Xwayland for X11 apps
- use the Plutonium helper and its agent bridge
- panel tab keys, new browser tab, app launcher
- thread tags, groups and the Elsewhere list
- what the user starts comes to the front; a toast for the rest
- agents drive windows and tabs
- recordings encode in a hidden page of Plutonium's browser; visible counts desktop-shown tabs
- Preview tools: drag along a path; snapshot images in click coordinates; cursor follows a scaled tab
- Preview tools: a stuck action no longer wedges its tab
- incognito tabs on the desktop
- the dock: Super+1…9 slots for the terminal, apps and sites
- usage-limit warnings in orchestrator_capabilities
- preview recordings are captures every shell sees
- native windows are their threads' server tabs
